{
  "title": "Body, food and daily life",
  "note": "Pain is expressed with dolere, to hurt, and a dative of the person: Caput mihi dolet, my head hurts. Romans ate ientaculum (breakfast), prandium (lunch) and the main meal, cena, in the late afternoon. Do not confuse os, oris (n), mouth, with os, ossis (n), bone.",
